 the latest month.","The price sits mid-way through its 52-week range, 8% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 48% and a beta of 1.37, it amplifies market moves, though its beta has shifted (1y 0.49 vs 5y 1.58), so read it loosely.","Liquidity is deep, with about $554.3M traded a day.","In past sell-offs it fell 83% in the 2020 crash, 64% in the 2022 bear market and 87% in 2008."],"val":["The price sits above its DCF fair value of $192 (margin of safety -70%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 22%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $105 to $336 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks expensive against Consumer Cyclical peers: EV/EBITDA 15.2 vs 11.2 and P/FCF 70.8 vs 16.5 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 20% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of 1.4% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 4.5% (vs the 8% bar).","The 26 covering analysts target $353 on average, 8% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 11% earns above the cost of capital of 10.2%, but the 1pp spread is short of the 7pp moat bar; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 2.10).","It converts 7% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 1.51x.","ROE of 43% is amplified by 4.1x balance-sheet leverage (DuPont), so ROIC is the cleaner read on the business.","Operating margin is running 59pp above its own historical average, a peak-margin risk if conditions normalise.","It spends 1.0% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is heavy at 3.1x net debt to EBITDA ($825.0M of cash against $21.3B of debt), with interest covered 4.9x.","The current ratio of 0.18 means short-term liabilities exceed current assets.","It runs on negative working capital (-21 days), so customers and suppliers effectively fund its operations."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 26.6% over 3 years and 52.0% over 5 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 126%).","At current returns, reinvesting 37% of profits supports about 4.2% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Margins are expanding (+1.1% trend).","Forward indicators: deferred revenue up 4%.","Capex runs 3.0x depreciation (29.2% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth.","Its Rule of 40 score is 58, clearing the bar for a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own 6.2%, meaningful skin in the game, and institutions hold 85%.","Insiders have only sold over the past year (91 sales, net $545.4M sold).","It returns 2.3% a year to shareholders (1.3% in buybacks and 1.8% in dividends).","The share count has grown 1.0% a year over five years, diluting existing holders."],"people":["With about 107,950 employees, each generates about $166K of revenue, 0.4x the Consumer Cyclical median, and productivity has risen 6.7% a year.","That works out to $11K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $8.2M (49x revenue per employee).","Stock compensation averages $2K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":40,"head":"Watch: priced 70% above its $192 fair value, but that value is low-confidence and the price is inside its $105\u2013$336 range.","pros":["Revenue grew 52.0%/yr over 5y","12-1 month momentum +16%","Operating margin expanding 1.1%/yr"],"cons":["Trades 70% above fair value of $192","Net debt/EBITDA 3.1x","Fair value is low-confidence (wide Monte Carlo spread)","EV/EBITDA 15.2x vs sector 11.2x","P/FCF 70.8x vs sector 16.5x"],"flags":[],"need":["the model rates it HOLD","no margin of safety","the fair value is low-confidence (wide Monte Carlo spread)","too few checks pass (conviction 40)"],"buy_below":163.15,"vc":{"base":191.94,"base_src":"dcf","bear":105.09,"bull":335.98,"alt_median":302.27,"n_alt":1,"gap":-0.365,"dispersion":0.2232,"level":"LOW","why":["Monte Carlo spread is wide","bull case is 3.2x the bear case"]},"med":{"pe":19.2575,"ev_ebitda":11.198,"pfcf":16.4664,"pb":2.375,"roic":0.1281,"gross_margin":0.3475,"fcf_margin":0.0624,"div_yield":0.0228}},"ticker":"RCL","date":"2026-11-06"}